<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's net reserves up to $1.85 bln on March 7.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's net reserves up to $1.85 bln on March 7.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Friday its net international reserves stood at $1.85 billion on March 7, up $73 million from the week before.</p>
<p>The bank gave no reason for the rise.</p>
<p>In February 1997, international reserves fell $215 million.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.83 billion at the end of last year, up $274 million from the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
